{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"A\": \"Research transition-generation cost while preserving search order. In move_me/do_move, compare precomputed legal neighbors against repeated coordinate division and boundary calculations. Compare per-expansion box occupancy lookup against repeated linear box scans; avoid clearing the whole board for every state. Walking moves need no box sorting. For pushes, replace bubble passes with insertion repair while reproducing the existing representation: the current loop sorts c[1..n_boxes-1] and leaves c[n_boxes] distinguished. Do not silently canonicalize all boxes. Preserve right, left, up, down generation order, uppercase push reporting, and valid-input boundary behavior. Produce incremental candidates so measurements distinguish neighbor, occupancy, and sorting effects. Coordinate allocation and hashing changes with B rather than independently replacing them.\",\n  \"B\": \"Research visited-set and state-storage efficiency. First measure restoring the cached-hash equality check before memcmp. Then investigate a better-mixed hash and open-addressed table with full state equality on collisions. Probe reusable candidate storage before allocating a permanent state, reducing duplicate allocation/recycling and writes. Separately investigate compact arena indices for parents and frontier links, with natural alignment on ARM64, checked sizing, and no new board-size or state-count restrictions. Hash-table layout must not determine expansion order. If replacing linked frontiers with arrays, reproduce the current whole-level reversal caused by head insertion, first-discovery parents, and immediate goal recognition. Preserve the actual source key representation. Submit hashing and storage changes separately before combining them.\",\n  \"C\": \"Research sound deadlock pruning without changing move-level BFS. Start with cheap push-local checks: a fully blocked 2-by-2 region of walls/boxes containing an off-goal box is permanently deadlocked. A more ambitious candidate should compute per-goal reverse-push reachability through static walls, extending the existing union live map, then reject configurations lacking a matching that assigns every box to a distinct reachable goal. Use the reference success condition; do not assume equal box and goal counts. These are necessary-condition relaxations, not heuristic declarations of failure. Evaluate expensive checks only when box positions change and measure their preprocessing/search tradeoff. Preserve relative order among surviving states. Do not substitute push-count search, merge player positions by reachable region, freeze boxes merely because they occupy goals, or introduce unproved deadlock patterns.\",\n  \"G\": \"Integrate only candidates produced by A/B/C, retaining the valid baseline and best standalone program. Use the unchanged correctness and timing harness within existing budgets. Check exact path bytes, push capitalization, initial success, frontier exhaustion, and collision handling; four passing cases do not replace general correctness arguments. Reconcile A's candidate generation with B's scratch lookup and C's push-only checks, and preserve reference traversal and predecessor selection. Measure selected combinations independently: pruning changes table occupancy, occupancy construction changes transition costs, and preprocessing can erase search savings. Never assume additive gains or automatically choose the largest combination. Prefer the simplest reliably faster valid candidate; retain baseline if no improvement is established. Do not change tests, oracle, compiler, target, permissions, or budgets, and never specialize to measured puzzle values.\",\n  \"analysis\": \"The supplied source targets Problem C, Sokoban. This run provides only a valid baseline: four correctness cases and a 4.894 ms mean, with samples spanning 4.837–4.983 ms. There is no hotspot profile or evidence of larger workloads. Candidate costs visible in the source include repeated box scans, coordinate arithmetic, sorting, duplicate-state allocation, and pointer-heavy hashing; these are hypotheses, not measured bottlenecks. At this latency, preprocessing and thread startup may outweigh savings, so prioritize serial improvements on the four-core ARM64 target. Exact-output compatibility is unusually important: moves are generated right/left/up/down, and each next frontier is prepended, reversing generation order between levels. This is not ordinary FIFO BFS in the statement's up/down/left/right order. The box-sort loop also excludes the final box slot. Replacing traversal or canonicalization casually can change the selected path despite preserving solvability and shortest length. A addresses transition cost, B storage and deduplication, and C provably safe state-space reduction.\"\n}"}}
